    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i've been trying out that box breathing thing (4 in, 4 hold, 4 out, 4 hold) to help with stress. can you explain what's actually happening in my body when i do that? like, how does it affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing activates your vagus nerve, which shifts your body out of the \"fight or flight\" state and into the \"rest and digest\" mode. This physiological shift slows your heart rate and signals your adrenal glands to stop releasing stress hormones like cortisol. Over time, this consistent practice can help retrain your nervous system to respond more calmly to stressful situations.",
      "source": "target",
