    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that. it's just a bit hard to explain, it feels almost like something else is driving that restlessness, like it's an external force or something. does science have any way to explain that feeling of losing control over your own body's rhythms like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, science explains this as \"autonomic dysregulation,\" where your involuntary nervous system takes over and moves faster than your conscious mind can control it. When adrenaline surges, it creates a feeling of being \"driven\" by internal biological rhythms you cannot stop, which mimics the sensation of an external force. Techniques like box breathing serve as a feedback loop to the brainstem, gradually teaching your nervous system to harmonize with your own slower, voluntary rhythms.",
      "source": "target",
